{"The test does not wait for the background thread to finish before asserting, which can make the test racey and flaky. The assertion runs immediately after starting the thread, so it can execute before the read loop runs, masking failures. Need to keep a reference to the Thread and wait for it to finish via join() with a timeout or a CountDownLatch/ExecutorService.": 0.8886677026748657, "If a deletion throws, the deletedAll flag is never set and the background thread may run indefinitely, leaking the thread and making the test unstable. Move deletedAll.set(true) into a finally block to ensure the reader thread can exit even if deletions fail.": 0.9342805743217468, "Using deletedAll.set(true) only after the delete loop means the reader thread may still run briefly after all deletions are done; coordinating shutdown via a latch or barrier would make the termination behavior more deterministic": 0.7214859127998352}